---
const steps = [
  {
    n: '01',
    key: 'clarify',
    title: 'Clarify',
    body: 'px0 asks only what would change the file: which channel, which repo, how often. Press Enter to skip; it never interrogates you.',
    accent: 'var(--cyan)',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    key: 'discover',
    title: 'Discover',
    body: 'It writes searches, not tool names, and looks them up across Composio’s catalogue: thousands of tools, not a curated ten.',
    accent: 'var(--violet)',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    key: 'confirm',
    title: 'Confirm',
    body: 'You see every tool it picked, with read / write access stated from the provider’s own metadata, before anything is authorized.',
    accent: 'var(--amber)',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    key: 'plan',
    title: 'Plan',
    body: 'It writes the workflow against exactly those tools, validates the cron and the inputs, and saves a Markdown file you can edit.',
    accent: 'var(--green)',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="how">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">px0 workflows new</span>
      <h2 class="h-section">Four passes.<br />One file you own.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        Turning a sentence into something that can post to Slack at 5pm on a Friday is not
        one prompt. px0 splits it into four passes, each small enough to do well, and stops
        for you at the two points where a wrong answer would actually cost you something.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <li class="step card reveal" style={`--accent:${s.accent}`}>
          <span class="step-n">{s.n}</span>
          <h3>{s.title}</h3>
          <p>{s.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="how-notes reveal">
      <div class="note">
        <span class="mark mark--write">write</span>
        <p>
          A tool that can post, send, or change anything outside px0 is called out by name
          before the workflow is written. Drop the ones you did not ask for.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        <span class="chip">--dry-run</span>
        <p>
          Resolve every input, stub every write. See exactly what a workflow would do before
          it does it for real.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        <span class="chip">px0 workflows edit</span>
        <p>
          Revising the sentence rebuilds the tools, inputs, and guidelines together, so they
          never drift out of sync with what you asked for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  .step {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: 26px 22px 24px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .step::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--accent), transparent);
    opacity: 0.5;
    transition: opacity 0.3s;
  }

  .step:hover::before { opacity: 1; }

  .step:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 34%, transparent);
  }

  .step-n {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }

  .step h3 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }

  .step p {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--txt-2);
  }

  .how-notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 34px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bdr);
  }

  .note {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .note p {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--txt-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .step-n { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .how-notes { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 22px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .steps { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
